    height: 2392
    caption: Ancient Roman road located in Syria which connected Antioch and Chalcis
  - file: Argenteus-Constantius_I-antioch_RIC_033a.jpg
    src: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Argenteus-Constantius_I-antioch_RIC_033a.jpg/250px-Argenteus-Constantius_I-antioch_RIC_033a.jpg
    width: 750
    height: 392
    caption: This argenteus was struck in the Antioch mint, under Constantius Chlorus.
  - file: Domitian_Tetradrachm_1.jpg
    src: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Domitian_Tetradrachm_1.jpg/250px-Domitian_Tetradrachm_1.jpg
    width: 946
    height: 465
    caption: Rare Domitian Tetradrachm struck in the Antioch Mint. Only 23 known
      examples. Note the realist portrait, typical of the Antioch Mint.
  - file: Amazonomachy_Antioch_Louvre_Ma3457.jpg
    src: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Amazonomachy_Antioch_Louvre_Ma3457.jpg/250px-Amazonomachy_Antioch_Louvre_Ma3457.jpg
    width: 3400
    height: 2266
    caption: A Greek rider seizes a mounted Amazonian warrior (armed with a
      double-headed axe) by her Phrygian cap; Roman mosaic emblema (marble and
      limestone), 2nd half of the 4th century AD; from Daphne, a suburb of
      Antioch-on-the-Orontes (now Antakya in Turkey.)
  - file: The_Antioch_Chalice,_first_half_of_6th_century,_Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art.jpg
    src: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/The_Antioch_Chalice%2C_first_half_of_6th_century%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art.jpg/250px-The_Antioch_Chalice%2C_first_half_of_6th_century%2C_Metropolitan_Museum_of_Art.jpg
    width: 470
    height: 590
    caption: The Antioch Chalice, first half of 6th century, Metropolitan Museum of Art
  - file: JulianusII-antioch(360-363)-CNG.jpg
    src: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/JulianusII-antioch%28360-363%29-CNG.jpg/250px-JulianusII-antioch%28360-363%29-CNG.jpg
    width: 287
    height: 294
    caption: A bronze coin from Antioch depicting the emperor Julian. Note the
